Inheritance

One class acquiring the properties and methods of another class.

class Animal {
    void eat() {
        System.out.println("Eating");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() {
        System.out.println("Barking");
    }
}

Polymorphism

One method or interface can have different implementations.

Types:

Compile-time polymorphism – Method Overloading

Runtime polymorphism – Method Overriding

Abstraction

Hiding implementation details and exposing essential functionality.

Achieved using:

Abstract classes

Interfaces

3. String

String is immutable in Java.

String name = "Java";
name.concat(" Developer");

System.out.println(name); // Java

To retain the result:

name = name.concat(" Developer");

StringBuilder:

Mutable

Not synchronized

Generally faster for single-threaded modifications

StringBuffer:

Mutable

Synchronized

Suitable when synchronized string modification is required

